(Phase A: `times` as a multiplication alias for `multiply`.
 6 times 7 -> 42; a Set/variable form; and a precedence check that
 prints the same expression with `times` and with `multiply` so the
 alias is proven identical.)

Print 6 times 7.
a number called n is 5.
Set n to n times 10.
Print n.
Print 2 plus 3 times 4.
Print 2 plus 3 multiply 4.